A||N||12||NOS3800||HPP Fiero Shootout||||4||
Z||000000||NOS3800||07-31-2001||12:08 AM||||High Perfoemance Pontiac is asking for people to send in photos for cars nterested in being in one of their shootouts. If you do not know what this is, the magazine gets 8-10 cars that are similar(Pontiacs of course) and take them to the drag strip and compare. This month they did late model Grand Prixs. I was thinking of mailing them a batch of interesting Fieros. In other words FAST ones! Thats what matters to this magazine. <BR>The tests are to be held at Englishtown Raceway in NJ, so you will need to be willing to travel.<BR>Now, we send them the pics and they decide if they will run the comparison. If you think you have something fast, send a pic or two of your car and a brief description. We will compile the photos and send in one big envelope. Send to:<BR>Bill Sessions<BR>4824 Kingfisher Court<BR>Waldorf MD. 20603<BR>I will be at the Williamsburg show, so you can hand me pics there too. Lets show them that Fieros can be fast!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||4
Z||000001||My7Fieros||07-31-2001||12:15 AM||||Hmmmm, sounds like a good idea. I used to subscribe to HPP about 10 years ago when I had my 78 Trans Am. I rarely read it anymore, mainly do to the fact that for some reason that magazine is very difficult to find (around here at least). Barnes and Noble is the only place Ive ever been able to find it....most anywhere else that stocks magazine doesnt for some strange reason.<BR>Ive also found that (in my limited recent readings in HPP) they dont seem to take well to Fieros. Sounds strange I know, but its usually all Firebirds, Formulas, and T/As, GTOs, older LeMans...muscle cars per say. I think Ive only seen one Fiero in that mag and that was back in 84 or 85. <BR>Still sounds like a good idea though, I say go for it! <P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||NOS3800||07-31-2001||12:22 AM||||The magazine is now going monthly so maybe it will be easier to find. I think they are starting to catch on to the Fiero craze. They have a few pics of Fieros at the staging lights at the last Englishtown Pontiac day in this months issue. Also, at Maple Grove the announcer would not stop talking about how Jasons was the Fatest Fiero he had seen( I believe he worked for HPP). Curiously, he never made mention of my brothers SC3800 car which was running just as fast as Jason.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||07-31-2001||09:55 AM||||Sounds like a grand idea!  I'll throw in pics of my stock '88 Formula 5-speed so they can have a baseline for all the modded cars to compare against.  We should try to get a quad 4, 3.4 V6, 3800SC, and hopefully a SBC and a N*.  Maybe throw in some turbo'ed cars too.  That would give a great mix of the different Fieros available, especially if some of them have been re-bodied.  <P>I'm thinking a good mix:<BR>Jay's Northstar<BR>California Kid's SBC<BR>Roger's turbo "Ferarri" <BR>My Formula   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Chris West's turbo 3.4TDC<BR>Phil's 3800SC (duh - go for magazine #2, Phil!)<BR>NOS3800's car - gotta have someone on da juice.<BR>FieroSound or 88Formula's 3.4<BR>Lisa's GT (gotta represent the ladies, too)<BR>Tina's V8 (gotta represent the V8 ladies, too   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>I'm sure there's room for a few more, too.  Man, I'd gladly drive up to NJ for the shootout!  That would rock!<p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||10
